 "name": "The Cheshire Cat",
 "note": "Polygons in the rest pose (A1) pixels. Gothic sheets (the Horseman's style, as the Wolf Man), redrawn from the Cerberus-style kit (sources/old_style/). Baker Street's seat 3, drawn facing right and mirrored. The master is the rest pose's OWN head (kept clear of the tail); his front legs are the 'arms' (rest only); every other pose is a whole-figure frame with its own drawn head. Vanished parts are drawn as plain white. The 'prop' box is the felt below the rail, not a prop: his dark stripes are the wood's colour, so the paws lying on the felt are kept as drawn there (felt still cleared).",
 "what": {
  "A1": "Rest: sitting up, front paws on the table's edge, tail curled up beside him, the grin",
  "A2": "Peeking at his cards (right paw cupped low over the felt)",
  "A3": "Check: pats the felt with one paw",
  "A4": "Call: a paw slides forward along the felt",
  "A5": "Bet: a paw pushed well forward, grinning wider",
  "A6": "Fold: a lazy flick of the paw toward the middle",
  "B1": "All in: both paws push forward together",
  "B2": "Show: a paw turns palm up",
  "B3": "Big win: both front paws thrown up, the grin enormous (`win_big`)",
  "B4": "Fading away tail first: tail and body up to mid-chest gone, the rest floating",
  "B5": "His head drifts a little way off his shoulders (decoy for B4)",
  "B6": "Blinks one eye, then the other: one eye shut",
  "C1": "Washes a paw (decoy for B6)",
  "C2": "The tip of his tail twitches",
  "C3": "His tail sways lazily to the other side (decoy for C2)",
  "C4": "Grins at the dealer",
  "C5": "Only the grin left, floating where his mouth was (the end of B4)",
  "C6": "A slow, knowing look at the viewer",
  "D1": "Talking: one paw raised, explaining",
  "D2": "Facing a big bet: eyes narrowed to slits, the grin thinner",
  "D3": "Lost a pot: ears back, a lopsided grin, a shrug",
  "D4": "Crushing loss: ears flat, the grin gone for once, slumped (`lose_big`)",
  "D5": "Heads up: leaning in on both paws, eyes wide and bright",
  "D6": "Knocked out: half vanished, a cheery wave of one paw"
 },
